{"content_hash": "c6c5577f8f4a1732", "version_id": 449, "article_id": 45, "level_code": "ja_n2", "lang": "ja", "level": 4, "level_label": "N2 中高級", "title": "インドの名優ナナ・パテカル氏、75歳で急死", "title_zh": "印度著名演员纳纳·帕特卡突然去世，享年75岁", "has_translation": true, "topic": "culture", "source": "bbc_culture", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cj3vqr5rknpeo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1613462540041-ccd487c9a985?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8MTB8fG91dHNwb2tlbiUyMGluZGlhbiUyMGFjdG9yfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ1ODN8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by FlipClip Marketing on Unsplash", "author": "FlipClip Marketing", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@flipclip?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/man-in-black-tank-top-covering-his-face-with-his-hand-AqmETAMl324?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(21, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(59, 46%, 48%)", "label": "CULTURE", "seed": "3b258fc8c3d4"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 256, "reading_minutes": 0.8, "lead": "インド映画界を代表する俳優ナナ・パテカル氏が75歳で亡くなった。ゴア州の自宅で意識を失い、病院に搬送されたが、心停止により死亡が確認された。", "lead_zh": "印度电影界代表性演员纳纳·帕特卡去世，享年75岁。他在果阿邦的家中失去意识，被送往医院后因心脏骤停被确认死亡。", "preview": "インドの著名な俳優ナナ・パテカル氏が8日、ゴア州で死去した。75歳だった。同氏は自宅で意識を失っているところを発見され、病院に運ばれたが、心停止により死亡が確認された。病院の医師によると、45分間の心肺蘇生にもかかわらず、蘇生しなかった。", "preview_zh": "印度著名演员纳纳·帕特卡于8日在果阿邦去世，享年75岁。他在家中被发现时已失去意识，被送往医院后因心脏骤停被确认死亡。据医院医生称，尽管进行了45分钟的心肺复苏，仍未能苏醒。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 439, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/45/ja_n2.mp3", "duration": 58.325, "size_bytes": 353664, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "ja-JP-NanamiNeural", "word_count": 177, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@0a373f3/content/data/versions/449.json", "paragraphs": ["インドの著名な俳優ナナ・パテカル氏が8日、ゴア州で死去した。75歳だった。同氏は自宅で意識を失っているところを発見され、病院に運ばれたが、心停止により死亡が確認された。病院の医師によると、45分間の心肺蘇生にもかかわらず、蘇生しなかった。", "パテカル氏は1978年の映画『ガマン』でデビューし、1989年の『パリンダー』でギャングのアンナ役を演じて全国的に有名になった。その後、『クランティヴィール』や『アグニ・サクシ』などで3度の国家映画賞を受賞。マラーティー語の映画や演劇でも活躍した。", "同氏は社会活動家としても知られ、農民支援や水資源保全に取り組んだ。2015年にはナーム財団を設立。"], "paragraphs_zh": ["印度著名演员纳纳·帕特卡于8日在果阿邦去世，享年75岁。他在家中被发现时已失去意识，被送往医院后因心脏骤停被确认死亡。据医院医生称，尽管进行了45分钟的心肺复苏，仍未能苏醒。", "帕特卡于1978年凭借电影《加曼》出道，1989年在《帕林达》中饰演黑帮分子安娜而全国闻名。此后，他凭借《革命者》和《烈火证人》等影片三次获得国家电影奖。他还在马拉地语电影和戏剧领域活跃。", "他还以社会活动家身份为人所知，致力于农民支援和水资源保护。2015年，他成立了纳姆基金会。另一方面，2018年女演员塔努什里·达塔指控他性骚扰，成为印度#MeToo运动的导火索之一。他否认指控，并于2019年因证据不足未被起诉。"], "body": "インドの著名な俳優ナナ・パテカル氏が8日、ゴア州で死去した。75歳だった。同氏は自宅で意識を失っているところを発見され、病院に運ばれたが、心停止により死亡が確認された。病院の医師によると、45分間の心肺蘇生にもかかわらず、蘇生しなかった。\n\nパテカル氏は1978年の映画『ガマン』でデビューし、1989年の『パリンダー』でギャングのアンナ役を演じて全国的に有名になった。その後、『クランティヴィール』や『アグニ・サクシ』などで3度の国家映画賞を受賞。マラーティー語の映画や演劇でも活躍した。\n\n同氏は社会活動家としても知られ、農民支援や水資源保全に取り組んだ。2015年にはナーム財団を設立。", "body_zh": "印度著名演员纳纳·帕特卡于8日在果阿邦去世，享年75岁。他在家中被发现时已失去意识，被送往医院后因心脏骤停被确认死亡。据医院医生称，尽管进行了45分钟的心肺复苏，仍未能苏醒。\n\n帕特卡于1978年凭借电影《加曼》出道，1989年在《帕林达》中饰演黑帮分子安娜而全国闻名。此后，他凭借《革命者》和《烈火证人》等影片三次获得国家电影奖。他还在马拉地语电影和戏剧领域活跃。\n\n他还以社会活动家身份为人所知，致力于农民支援和水资源保护。2015年，他成立了纳姆基金会。另一方面，2018年女演员塔努什里·达塔指控他性骚扰，成为印度#MeToo运动的导火索之一。他否认指控，并于2019年因证据不足未被起诉。", "text": "インドの著名な俳優ナナ・パテカル氏が8日、ゴア州で死去した。75歳だった。同氏は自宅で意識を失っているところを発見され、病院に運ばれたが、心停止により死亡が確認された。病院の医師によると、45分間の心肺蘇生にもかかわらず、蘇生しなかった。 パテカル氏は1978年の映画『ガマン』でデビューし、1989年の『パリンダー』でギャングのアンナ役を演じて全国的に有名になった。その後、『クランティヴィール』や『アグニ・サクシ』などで3度の国家映画賞を受賞。マラーティー語の映画や演劇でも活躍した。 同氏は社会活動家としても知られ、農民支援や水資源保全に取り組んだ。2015年にはナーム財団を設立。", "vocab": [{"word": "死去", "pos": "noun", "zh": "去世", "note": "正式表达，比「死ぬ」更客观"}, {"word": "心肺蘇生", "pos": "noun", "zh": "心肺复苏", "note": "医疗术语，常与「行う」搭配"}, {"word": "心停止", "pos": "noun", "zh": "心脏骤停", "note": "医学用语"}, {"word": "デビュー", "pos": "noun", "zh": "出道", "note": "常用外来语"}, {"word": "受賞", "pos": "noun", "zh": "获奖", "note": "常与「する」搭配"}, {"word": "活躍", "pos": "noun", "zh": "活跃", "note": "常与「する」搭配"}, {"word": "社会活動家", "pos": "noun", "zh": "社会活动家", "note": ""}, {"word": "疑惑", "pos": "noun", "zh": "嫌疑、指控", "note": "常与「告げられる」搭配"}, {"word": "否定", "pos": "noun", "zh": "否认", "note": "常与「する」搭配"}, {"word": "不起訴", "pos": "noun", "zh": "不予起诉", "note": "法律术语"}, {"word": "追悼", "pos": "noun", "zh": "追悼", "note": "常与「の意を表す」搭配"}, {"word": "葬儀", "pos": "noun", "zh": "葬礼", "note": ""}, {"word": "国葬", "pos": "noun", "zh": "国葬", "note": ""}, {"word": "遺灰", "pos": "noun", "zh": "骨灰", "note": ""}], "title_original": "Outspoken Indian actor Nana Patekar dies suddenly at 75", "summary_original": "Known for his intense performances, Patekar carved out a distinctive place in Indian cinema.", "body_original": "Outspoken Indian actor Nana Patekar dies suddenly at 75\nBy\nVikas Pandey\nBBC News, Delhi\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nVeteran Indian actor Nana Patekar, known for his intense, fiery performances on stage and in film, has died at the age of 75 in Goa.\nOne of the most recognisable faces of Indian cinema, Patekar won three National Film Awards and became known for playing difficult and often volatile characters. He was also a prominent figure in Marathi language cinema and theatre.\nHe was admitted to a hospital after being found unconscious at his home in Goa in the early hours of Thursday.\n\"Despite 45 minutes of continuous CPR, he could not be revived,\" Dr Shekhar Salkar of Manipal Hospital in Goa told ANI news agency. Tributes have poured in from actors and politicians across India.\nDr Salkar later told PTI news agency that the hospital team found Patekar at his home \"unconscious and almost unresponsive\".\nThe team continued giving him CPR even while taking him to the hospital, located about 10 minutes away, but he was dead by the time they reached there, he added.\nDr Salkar said Patekar had suffered a cardiac arrest, but it was not clear what had triggered it.\nFamily, friends and fans paid their last respects to the actor at Goa Medical College, ahead of his funeral which was to take place later in the day with full state honours at his farm house in the western city of Pune in Maharashtra state.\nIn the evening, his remains were flown to Pune by air ambulance, where the state's chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis paid his last respects, before Patekar's body was taken to his farm in Donje village where last rites were performed and he was cremated.\nTimes of India reports that his son, Malhar, told reporters afterwards that his father has not truly gone anywhere and will to remain with them - even if not physically - and his commitment to social welfare would live on.\nEarlier, Prime Minister Narendra Modi led tributes to the actor, praising Patekar's versatility and outspoken personality.\nPatekar portrayed characters that would \"remain etched in the memory of generations\", Modi wrote on X, adding that his death had left \"a vast void in the artistic world\".\nBollywood veteran Anupam Kher paid tribute to his friend on social media, saying he would miss his warmth and extraordinary performances and called him \"one of the finest actors and human beings in Indian cinema\".\nAnother Bollywood star Shah Rukh Khan called him \"a mentor, a teacher, a critic and a friend\", adding that Patekar has \"left a void not only in the world of cinema but in the hearts of all Indians and the world\".\nAkshay Kumar, who appeared alongside Patekar in the comedy film Welcome, remembered him as a rare performer whose voice, intensity and honesty could command an audience's attention.\nPatekar made his debut with the film Gaman in 1978 and continued to play smaller roles in several films. But the intensity that he brought on the screen was hard to miss and soon he landed a role in Parinda in 1989, making him a household name across India. He won his first National Film Award and the Filmfare Award as well for his portrayal of the gangster Anna in the film.\nHe didn't look back after this and portrayed many memorable roles in films in the 1990s. The range of characters he played showcased the depth of his acting talent and mastery of his craft.\nFamous dialogues from his films, delivered in his inimitable rasping voice, were quoted in school corridors and tea stalls. Many professional comedians imitate his distinctive style even today.\n\"He had a distinctive style of working and how he approached characters. As a person, he was outspoken and difficult to get along with but directors would still want to work with him because he was simply a fantastic actor,\" film trade analyst Komal Nahta told BBC.\nHis portrayal of Major Chauhan in Prahaar – a film he also directed – won him praise. His other characters, including the patriotic hero of Tirangaa and Pratap Narayan Tilak in Krantiveer, also won him accolades.\nJust when critics thought that playing loud characters was his mainstay, he proved them wrong by delivering a mesmerising performance in Khamoshi as a person who could not hear or speak.\nDirector Prakash Jha's Rajneeti in 2010 added another dimension to his acting as his portrayal of an astute politician was delivered with perfection.\nThe breadth of Patekar's career showcases the wide range of his work. He played different but contrasting roles like that of a notorious gangster or a policeman with equal ease. He also sometimes worked behind the camera as a director and writer.\nHis three national awards for Parinda, Krantiveer and Agni Sakshi are testament to his wide-ranging career.\nPatekar was an influential figure too in both Marathi and Hindi theatre. Before making his debut in films, he was involved in theatre, where he developed his gritty style of dialogue delivery and also mastered the intensity he brought to his on-screen characters.\nPurush and Hamidabai Chi Kothi were two of his most famous plays. Despite being successful in films, he remained active in theatre throughout his professional life.\nPatekar was known for his activism and didn't mince his words while criticising the government of the day. He was direct, and almost brazen and unapologetic, when it came to criticising ministers and their policies - and did so quite publicly.\nIssues related to farmers were particularly close to his heart.\nHis work went beyond just giving statements. In 2015 he and actor Makarand Anaspure established the Naam Foundation, which has worked on farmer welfare and water conservation in Maharashtra.\nBut his career was not without controversies.\nIn 2018, allegations of sexual harassment made by actor Tanushree Dutta against Patekar over an alleged incident on a film set a decade earlier helped spark\nIndia's #MeToo movement\n. Patekar denied the allegations.\nIn 2019, he was cleared of the charges after police said they had not found sufficient evidence against him.\nAdditional reporting by Rachita Prasad\nRelated topics\nIndia\nAsia\nBollywood\nMaharashtra", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:09:41.810702", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "インド", "s": 0.125, "e": 0.487, "sm": 125, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "の", "s": 0.5, "e": 0.625, "sm": 500, "em": 625, "cs": 3, "ce": 4, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "著名", "s": 0.637, "e": 1.05, "sm": 637, "em": 1049, "cs": 4, "ce": 6, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "な", "s": 1.062, "e": 1.163, "sm": 1062, "em": 1162, "cs": 6, "ce": 7, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "俳優", "s": 1.175, "e": 1.638, "sm": 1175, "em": 1637, "cs": 7, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "ナナ", "s": 1.65, "e": 1.95, "sm": 1650, "em": 1950, "cs": 9, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "・", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.212, "sm": 1950, "em": 2212, "cs": 11, "ce": 12, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "パテカル", "s": 2.212, "e": 2.725, "sm": 2212, "em": 2724, "cs": 12, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "氏", "s": 2.737, "e": 2.875, "sm": 2737, "em": 2875, "cs": 16, "ce": 17, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "が", "s": 2.888, "e": 2.975, "sm": 2887, "em": 2975, "cs": 17, "ce": 18, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "8", "s": 2.987, "e": 3.25, "sm": 2987, "em": 3250, "cs": 18, "ce": 19, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "日", "s": 3.25, "e": 3.512, "sm"